WEBVTT

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.720
I'm so sorry, dear.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.000
He was my best mate.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.000
What happened here?

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.600
This is what becomes
of those who cross the Witch.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.240
You take one more step, traitor,
and I'll chew you to splinters!

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.480
Relax. I'm one of the good guys.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.600
Yeah? Well, you look an awful lot
like one of the bad ones.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.040
An unfortunate family resemblance.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.480
But we can argue breeding later.
Right now we've got to move.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:45.720
(WOLVES APPROACHING)

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.920
What did you have in mind?

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.400
(SNARLING)

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.200
Greetings, gents.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.000
-Lost something, have we?
-Don't patronise me!

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.000
I know where your allegiance lies.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.320
We're looking for some humans.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.000
(CHUCKLING) Humans?
Here in Narnia?

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.400
That's a valuable bit of information,
don't you think?

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:13.600
(SNARLING)

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.760
(WHINING)

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.880
Your reward is your life.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.760
It's not much,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.720
but still.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.320
Where are the fugitives?

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.000
(PANTING) North. They ran north.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.800
Smell them out.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.320
They were helping Tumnus.
The Witch got here before I did.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.480
Ow!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.320
Are you all right?

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.960
Well, I wish I could say their bark
was worse than their bite.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.120
Ow!

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.240
Stop squirming!
You're worse than Beaver on bath day.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:04.960
Worst day of the year.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.520
Thank you for your kindness,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.360
but that's all the cure I have time for.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.520
You're leaving?

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:14.360
It has been a pleasure, My Queen,
and an honour, but time is short

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.440
and Aslan himself has asked me
to gather more troops.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.600
-You've seen Aslan?
-What's he like?

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.320
Like everything we've ever heard.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.320
You'll be glad to have him by your side
in the battle against the Witch.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.440
But we're not planning
on fighting any witch.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.200
But surely, King Peter, the prophecy!

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.680
We can't go to war without you.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.080
We just want our brother back.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.480
(COUGHING)

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.080
TUMNUS: If...

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.600
If you're not going to eat that...

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.360
I'd get up, but...

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.120
But my legs.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:27.960
(MOANING)

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.800
Mr. Tumnus.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.440
What's left of him.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.320
-You're Lucy Pevensie's brother.
-I'm Edmund.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.880
Yes. Yes, you have the same nose.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.160
Is your sister all right?

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.760
Is she safe?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.960
(WOLVES BARKING)

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.640
I don't know.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.000
(DOOR OPENS)

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.160
My police tore that dam apart.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.480
Your little family
are nowhere to be found.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.560
-Where did they go?
-I don't know!

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.280
Then you're of no further use to me.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.400
Wait! The beaver
said something about Aslan!

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.320
Aslan?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.840
Where?

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.640
-I...
-He's a stranger here, Your Majesty.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.440
He can't be expected to know anything.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:03.840
I said, where is Aslan?

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.720
I... I don't know.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.600
I left before they said anything.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.680
I wanted to see you!

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.720
Guard!

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.360
Your Majesty.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.120
Release the faun.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.520
(GRUNTS)

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.160
(TUMNUS GROANING)

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.800
Do you know why you're here, faun?

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.760
Because I believe in a free Narnia.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.480
You're here

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.360
because he turned you in.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.920
For sweeties.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.600
Take him upstairs.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:11.960
(GRUNTS)

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.880
And ready my sleigh.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.000
Edmund misses his family.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:47.840
Now, Aslan's camp
is near the Stone Table

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.920
-just across the frozen river.
-River?

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.480
The river's been frozen solid
for a hundred years.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.760
-It's so far.
-It's the world, dear.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.160
Did you expect it to be small?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.040
Smaller.

